    Route checkpoints through entire:// push-through mirrors

    When origin (or the push remote) is an entire:// mirror URL and its forge
    matches the configured checkpoint_remote provider (gh <-> github),
    derive the checkpoint URL on the same cluster
    (entire://<cluster>/<forge>/<checkpoint-repo>) instead of falling back
    to direct SSH/HTTPS against the provider host. The provider-host
    fallback remains for file:// and forge-mismatched mirrors, and
    ENTIRE_CHECKPOINT_TOKEN still forces provider HTTPS since the token
    cannot ride through the helper.

